                <pb facs="0345" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/2457: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-10-27T19:00:00+01:00">October 27, 1932—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 27—6 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>28. Your 25, October 26, 5 p.m. I have communicated substance of this telegram to
                        Drummond. He was happy to hear the
                    news it contains and stated that the Council committee when it learns of it will
                    appreciate highly the successful results which the Neutral Commission has
                    obtained. Drummond asks whether he may
                    assume that in due course the President of the Neutral Commission will
                    communicate this information formally to the President of the Council so that
                    the latter may impart it to his colleagues on the Committee of Three and
                    ultimately to the Council itself.</p>
                <p>Please instruct.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
